# Run producer.py every 12 hours — walks the configured source listing
# pages, creates draft articles via the Go API, and enqueues
# parsing.scrape_source (parsing_queue) for each genuinely new one. Only
# takes effect in the parser-producer service (infra/docker-compose.yml),
# which overrides this image's default CMD with `cron -f`; the plain
# `parser` service still runs the Celery consumer (see Dockerfile CMD).
#
# ". /etc/cron_env.sh": cron jobs run with a bare environment, not the
# container's — this sources the dump entrypoint.sh wrote at startup so
# GOLANG_API/CELERY_BROKER_URL/API_USER_* are actually set.
# ">> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1": with `cron -f` as this container's PID 1, writing
# straight to its own stdout/stderr is what makes output show up in
# `docker compose logs` — cron jobs are silent by default otherwise.
# "root": /etc/cron.d/* entries need an explicit user field (unlike a plain
# `crontab -e` file) — omitting it is why this line never actually ran.
0 */12 * * * root . /etc/cron_env.sh && python /app/producer.py >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
